#
# h713-tv's state that outlives a restart of the program but not the boot: "ctl mute" (MUTE_FILE in main.c).
# h713-tv is restarted after every standby that parked the display MIPS, by the rescue and after a crash, and a
# mute kept only in the program came back loud. Not in the unit's RuntimeDirectory, which systemd empties at every
# stop; on the tmpfs, so a cold start is audible again. Installed as /etc/tmpfiles.d/h713-tv.conf.
d /run/h713-tv-state 0755 root root -
